TEXTS = {
    'task29_golden_explanation.txt': '### Overview\n\nThe zip is a complete Lake project. `lakefile.toml` and `lake-manifest.json` use the pinned Mathlib checkout at `/opt/mathlib4` (commit `9944fe2973b8dc0b86949101ed98232c07cd54a0`), and `lean-toolchain` is `leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc1`. The proof sits in eight files under `TuringTask/` that import each other in a chain: `Regular`, `Units`, `Layers`, `Zolotarev`, `Power`, `Transpose`, `Main`, `Basic`. Every file starts with `import Mathlib`. The required file `TuringTask/Basic.lean` is the file of the prompt with one added line `import TuringTask.Main`. Its namespace and its five statements stay as in the prompt, and each `sorry` became a one-line `exact` of the matching theorem in `Main.lean`.\n\nIn this text $\\mu_a$ is $x \\mapsto ax$ on $\\mathbb{Z}/n$, $\\nu_a$ is $u \\mapsto au$ on the unit group $(\\mathbb{Z}/n)^\\times$, and $J(a \\mid n)$ is `jacobiSym a n`. For a finite group $G$ we write $N = |G|$.\n\nThe route:\n- (A) In a finite commutative group, left multiplication by $g$ of order $d$ consists of $N/d$ cycles of length $d$. So its sign is $-1$ exactly when $N$ is even and $g^{N/2} \\ne 1$.\n- (B) If $(\\mathbb{Z}/n)^\\times$ is cyclic, $g^{N/2} \\ne 1$ means that $g$ is not a square. If it is not cyclic, it has two different elements of order $2$, and then every sign is $1$. This gives theorem 3.\n- (C) On $\\mathbb{Z}/p^{k+1}$ the units and the multiples of $p$ are invariant sets, and the multiples of $p$ form a copy of $\\mathbb{Z}/p^k$. So $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a$ on $\\mathbb{Z}/p^k$ is the product of the signs of $\\nu_a$ on $(\\mathbb{Z}/p^j)^\\times$ for $1 \\le j \\le k$. The Chinese remainder theorem splits coprime moduli.\n- (D) For odd $p$ the sign of $\\nu_a$ on $(\\mathbb{Z}/p^j)^\\times$ is $J(a \\mid p)$, which gives theorem 1. For $p = 2$ only $(\\mathbb{Z}/4)^\\times$ contributes, which gives theorem 2. A generator of $(\\mathbb{Z}/p)^\\times$ turns $x \\mapsto x^k$ into $\\mu_k$ on $\\mathbb{Z}/(p-1)$, which gives theorem 4. Theorem 5 counts inversions.\n\n### 1. Regular.lean: signs of regular permutations\n\n- `cosetProd`: $G \\simeq (G/H) \\times H$, $x \\mapsto (xH, \\mathrm{out}(xH)^{-1} x)$.\n- `sign_mulLeft_zpowers`: on $H = \\langle g \\rangle$, left multiplication by $g$ is conjugate to `finRotate d` through `finEquivZPowers`, so its sign is $(-1)^{d-1}$ (`sign_finRotate`).\n- `sign_mulLeft`: for commutative $G$, `cosetProd` turns left multiplication by $g$ into `Equiv.prodCongrRight` of the map on $H$. With `Perm.sign_prodCongrRight` and $|G/H| = N/d$ the sign is $(-1)^{(d-1)N/d}$.\n- `sign_mulLeft_eq_neg_one_iff`: $(d - 1)N/d$ is odd iff $d$ is even and $N/d$ is odd, iff $N$ is even and $d \\nmid N/2$, that is $g^{N/2} \\ne 1$ (`odd_iff_aux`).\n- `isSquare_iff_pow_half`: in a cyclic group of even order, $g = \\gamma^r$ is a square iff $r$ is even iff $g^{N/2} = 1$.\n- `sign_mulLeft_of_two_involutions`: if the sign of $g$ is $-1$, then the index $N/d$ of $\\langle g \\rangle$ is odd. Every $x$ with $x^2 = 1$ then lies in $\\langle g \\rangle$, because $x = x^{N/d}$ (`Subgroup.pow_index_mem`). A cyclic group has at most one element of order $2$ (`IsCyclic.card_pow_eq_one_le`), so two different ones force the sign $1$.\n\n### 2. Units.lean: theorem 3\n\n- `list_iff` restates `ZMod.isCyclic_units_iff` for $n \\ne 0, 1, 2$: the group is cyclic iff $n$ is $4$, $p^k$ or $2p^k$.\n- `split_of_not_cyclic`: otherwise $n = 2^{e+3}$, or $n = ab$ with coprime $a, b \\ge 3$. Write $n = 2^e m$ with $m$ odd and $m = p^k r$ with $p \\nmid r$. Then $(a, b)$ is $(2^e, p^k)$ for $r = 1$ and $(2^e p^k, r)$ otherwise.\n- `exists_sqrt_one`: then some $x \\ne \\pm 1$ has $x^2 = 1$, namely $x = 1 + 2^{e+2}$, or $x \\equiv 1 \\pmod a$ and $x \\equiv -1 \\pmod b$ (`ZMod.chineseRemainder`).\n- `sign_units_iff`: for $n = 1, 2$ the group has one element. In the cyclic case $N = \\varphi(n)$ is even (`Nat.totient_even`), and (A) with `isSquare_iff_pow_half` gives the statement. In the other case $x$ and $-1$ are two different elements of order $2$, so the sign is $1$, and the right side fails because the group is not cyclic.\n\n### 3. Layers.lean: invariant pieces\n\n- `sign_split`: a permutation that keeps a set $P$ has sign $\\mathrm{sgn}(\\text{on } P) \\cdot \\mathrm{sgn}(\\text{off } P)$ (`Perm.sign_subtypeCongr`).\n- `sign_units_part`: on the units of $\\mathbb{Z}/n$, $\\mu_a$ is $\\nu_a$ (`unitsSubtypeEquiv`).\n- `not_isUnit_iff_dvd`, `layerEquiv`: the non-units of $\\mathbb{Z}/p^{k+1}$ are the elements $py$ with $y \\in \\mathbb{Z}/p^k$. `sign_layer`: since $p \\cdot (ay \\bmod p^k) \\equiv a p y \\pmod{p^{k+1}}$, this gives $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(p^{k+1}) = \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\nu_a(p^{k+1}) \\cdot \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(p^k)$.\n- `sign_prodCongr`: $\\mathrm{sgn}(\\sigma \\times \\tau) = \\mathrm{sgn}(\\sigma)^{|B|} \\mathrm{sgn}(\\tau)^{|A|}$. `sign_crt`: for coprime $m, n$, $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(mn) = \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(m)^n \\, \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(n)^m$.\n\n### 4. Zolotarev.lean: theorems 1 and 2\n\n- `sign_units_odd_prime_pow`: for an odd prime $p$ the group $(\\mathbb{Z}/p^j)^\\times$ is cyclic (`ZMod.isCyclic_units_of_prime_pow`) of order $N = p^{j-1}(p - 1)$. The element $g^{N/2}$ is $\\pm 1$, since a cyclic group has one element of order $2$. Modulo $p$ it equals $a^{p^{j-1}(p-1)/2} = a^{(p-1)/2} = J(a \\mid p)$ (`ZMod.pow_card_pow`, `legendreSym.eq_pow`). So $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\nu_a = J(a \\mid p)$.\n- `sign_odd_prime_pow`: by `sign_layer` and induction, $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(p^k) = J(a \\mid p)^k = J(a \\mid p^k)$ (`jacobiSym.pow_right`).\n- `sign_odd` (theorem 1): induction over coprime prime powers (`Nat.recOnPosPrimePosCoprime`) with `sign_crt`. For odd $m, n$ a sign to an odd power is the sign itself, and `jacobiSym.mul_right` finishes.\n- `sign_units_two`, `sign_units_four`, `sign_units_two_pow`: on $(\\mathbb{Z}/2)^\\times$ the sign is $1$, on $(\\mathbb{Z}/4)^\\times$ it is $1$ iff $a \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$, and on $(\\mathbb{Z}/2^j)^\\times$ with $j \\ge 3$ it is $1$, because that group is not cyclic (`ZMod.isCyclic_units_two_pow_iff` and theorem 3).\n- `sign_two_pow`: so $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(2^{k+1})$ is $1$ for $k = 0$ and the sign on $(\\mathbb{Z}/4)^\\times$ for $k \\ge 1$.\n- `sign_even` (theorem 2): for $n = 2^e m$ with $m$ odd and $e \\ge 1$, `sign_crt` gives $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(2^e)^m \\, \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(m)^{2^e} = \\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_a(2^e)$, and $n \\equiv 2 \\pmod 4$ iff $e = 1$.\n\n### 5. Power.lean: theorem 4\n\n- `sign_powMap`: a bijective $x \\mapsto x^k$ has $k \\ne 0$, keeps the units and fixes $0$, so only the units count. Let $m = p - 1$ and $e$ be an isomorphism from `Multiplicative (ZMod m)` onto $(\\mathbb{Z}/p)^\\times$ (`zmodCyclicMulEquiv`). Through $e$ the map becomes $y \\mapsto ky$ on $\\mathbb{Z}/m$ (`toAdd_pow`). Surjectivity gives $ky = 1$ for some $y$, so $k$ is prime to $m$, and the sign is $\\mathrm{sgn}\\,\\mu_k(p - 1)$. For $p = 2$ this is $1$. For odd $p$ theorem 2 gives $1$ when $p \\equiv 3 \\pmod 4$ and $(-1)^{(k-1)/2}$ when $p \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$.\n\n### 6. Transpose.lean: theorem 5\n\n- `sign_eq_neg_one_pow_card`: from `Perm.sign_eq_prod_prod_Iio`, the sign of a permutation $\\sigma$ of `Fin N` is $(-1)^I$, where $I$ counts the pairs $x < y$ with $\\sigma(y) < \\sigma(x)$.\n- `transposePerm` is the permutation of the statement. Position $j + ni$ holds the entry $(i, j)$ and goes to $i + mj$ (`transpose_val`).\n- `lex_lt`: for $j, j\' < n$, $j + ni < j\' + ni\'$ iff $i < i\'$, or $i = i\'$ and $j < j\'$. `inversion_iff`: the entries $(i, j)$ and $(i\', j\')$ form an inversion iff $i < i\'$ and $j\' < j$.\n- `card_lt_pairs`: `Fin m` has $\\sum_{j < m} j = \\binom{m}{2}$ pairs $i < i\'$ (`Finset.sum_range_id`). `card_inversions`: the inversions match the pairs $(i < i\', j\' < j)$, so $I = \\binom{m}{2}\\binom{n}{2}$ (`Finset.card_nbij\'`).\n\n### 7. Main.lean and Basic.lean\n\n- `main_odd`, `main_even`, `main_units`, `main_pow`, `main_transpose`: the five results in the form of the prompt.\n- In `Basic.lean` each of the five theorems is one `exact` of the matching theorem.\n\n### Verification\n\n- I extracted the final zip into a fresh folder and checked it offline, without editing anything, in the setting of the review environment: Mathlib at `/opt/mathlib4` (the pinned checkout, commit `9944fe2973b8dc0b86949101ed98232c07cd54a0`, with its dependencies linked into `.lake/packages` as `lean-offline-init` does), Lean `4.33.0-rc1`, network access blocked.\n- `lake build` ends with "Build completed successfully", exit code 0, with no errors and no warnings. Every file uses the full `import Mathlib`.\n- `lake env lean StatementAndAxiomsCheck.lean` (included in the zip) restates the five theorems of the prompt, so it fails if a statement changed. It reports exactly the axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` for each of the five theorems, with exit code 0.\n- The project contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `native_decide`, new axiom, `set_option` or instance declaration, and no declaration in `TuringTask` has the name of a Mathlib declaration.\n\n### Sources and related work\n\nTheorem 1 for a prime $n$ is G. Zolotarev, Nouvelle demonstration de la loi de reciprocite de Legendre, Nouv. Ann. Math. (2) 11 (1872), 354-362. The odd composite case is due to G. Frobenius, Uber das quadratische Reziprozitatsgesetz I, Sitzungsber. Preuss. Akad. Wiss. Berlin (1914), 335-349, and the even case to M. Lerch, Sur un theoreme de Zolotarev, Bull. Intern. Acad. Francois Joseph 3 (1896), 34-37. F. Lemmermeyer, Reciprocity Laws (Springer 2000), chapter 1, treats these results. The write-up and the Lean code are my own.\n\nThe proof uses these Mathlib results: `Perm.sign_eq_sign_of_equiv`, `Perm.sign_prodCongrRight`, `Perm.sign_prodCongrLeft`, `Perm.sign_subtypeCongr`, `sign_finRotate`, `Perm.sign_eq_prod_prod_Iio`, `finEquivZPowers`, `Subgroup.pow_index_mem`, `IsCyclic.card_pow_eq_one_le`, `ZMod.isCyclic_units_iff`, `ZMod.isCyclic_units_of_prime_pow`, `ZMod.isCyclic_units_two_pow_iff`, `zmodCyclicMulEquiv`, `ZMod.chineseRemainder`, `ZMod.card_units_eq_totient`, `legendreSym.eq_pow` and `jacobiSym.pow_right`. Mathlib at the pinned commit has `Equiv.Perm.sign` and the cyclic-units criterion, but nothing that links signs of permutations with Jacobi symbols. I found no Lean formalization of the five statements in Mathlib, `TauCetiProject/TauCeti`, `AllenGrahamHart/FormalConjectures-Bench`, formal-conjectures, compfiles, PutnamBench, miniF2F or ProofNet, or by web search (checked 14 Oct 2026).\n\nThe golden answer shows one valid route. Any complete proof of the five statements is acceptable.\n',
    'task29_rubric.csv': '"ID","Criterion","Weight"\n"1","`lake build` of the submitted project finishes without errors with Lean toolchain `leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc1` and Mathlib commit `9944fe2973b8dc0b86949101ed98232c07cd54a0`, and the build includes the module `TuringTask.Basic` from the file `TuringTask/Basic.lean`. This item checks only the build. Items 2 to 6 check the theorems.","1"\n"2","The project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_eq_jacobiSym (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 1) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) = jacobiSym a n`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_eq_jacobiSym` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.","1"\n"3","The project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_of_even (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 0) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) = if n % 4 = 2 then 1 else if a % 4 = 1 then 1 else -1`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_of_even` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.","1"\n"4","The project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_units_eq_neg_one_iff (n : Nat) [NeZero n] (u : Units (ZMod n)) : Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.mulLeft u) = -1 <-> (n = 4 \\/ exists p k : Nat, p.Prime /\\ p % 2 = 1 /\\ 0 < k /\\ (n = p ^ k \\/ n = 2 * p ^ k)) /\\ Not (IsSquare u)`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_units_eq_neg_one_iff` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.","1"\n"5","The project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_ofBijective_pow (p k : Nat) [NeZero p] (hp : p.Prime) (hk : Function.Bijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k)) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.ofBijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k) hk) : Int) = if p % 4 = 1 /\\ k % 4 = 3 then -1 else 1`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_ofBijective_pow` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.","1"\n"6","The project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_transpose (m n : Nat) : (Equiv.Perm.sign ((finProdFinEquiv.symm.trans (Equiv.prodComm (Fin m) (Fin n))).trans (finProdFinEquiv.trans (finCongr (Nat.mul_comm n m)))) : Int) = (-1) ^ (Nat.choose m 2 * Nat.choose n 2)`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_transpose` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.","1"',
    'task29_rubric.txt': '`lake build` of the submitted project finishes without errors with Lean toolchain `leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc1` and Mathlib commit `9944fe2973b8dc0b86949101ed98232c07cd54a0`, and the build includes the module `TuringTask.Basic` from the file `TuringTask/Basic.lean`. This item checks only the build. Items 2 to 6 check the theorems.\nThe project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_eq_jacobiSym (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 1) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) = jacobiSym a n`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_eq_jacobiSym` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.\nThe project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_of_even (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 0) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) = if n % 4 = 2 then 1 else if a % 4 = 1 then 1 else -1`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_of_even` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.\nThe project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_units_eq_neg_one_iff (n : Nat) [NeZero n] (u : Units (ZMod n)) : Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.mulLeft u) = -1 <-> (n = 4 \\/ exists p k : Nat, p.Prime /\\ p % 2 = 1 /\\ 0 < k /\\ (n = p ^ k \\/ n = 2 * p ^ k)) /\\ Not (IsSquare u)`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_mulLeft_units_eq_neg_one_iff` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.\nThe project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_ofBijective_pow (p k : Nat) [NeZero p] (hp : p.Prime) (hk : Function.Bijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k)) : (Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.ofBijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k) hk) : Int) = if p % 4 = 1 /\\ k % 4 = 3 then -1 else 1`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_ofBijective_pow` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.\nThe project contains a complete proof of `theorem TuringTask.sign_transpose (m n : Nat) : (Equiv.Perm.sign ((finProdFinEquiv.symm.trans (Equiv.prodComm (Fin m) (Fin n))).trans (finProdFinEquiv.trans (finCongr (Nat.mul_comm n m)))) : Int) = (-1) ^ (Nat.choose m 2 * Nat.choose n 2)`. The declaration has exactly this statement, and `#print axioms TuringTask.sign_transpose` lists only axioms from `{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`, so the list does not contain `sorryAx`. This item checks only this theorem. Item 1 checks the build of the whole project.\n',
}

PROMPT_BASIC = 'import Mathlib\n\nnamespace TuringTask\n\ntheorem sign_mulLeft_eq_jacobiSym (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 1) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) :\n    (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) = jacobiSym a n := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem sign_mulLeft_of_even (n a : Nat) [NeZero n] (hn : n % 2 = 0) (ha : Nat.Coprime a n) :\n    (Equiv.Perm.sign (Units.mulLeft (ZMod.unitOfCoprime a ha)) : Int) =\n      if n % 4 = 2 then 1 else if a % 4 = 1 then 1 else -1 := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem sign_mulLeft_units_eq_neg_one_iff (n : Nat) [NeZero n] (u : Units (ZMod n)) :\n    Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.mulLeft u) = -1 <->\n      (n = 4 \\/\n        exists p k : Nat, p.Prime /\\ p % 2 = 1 /\\ 0 < k /\\ (n = p ^ k \\/ n = 2 * p ^ k)) /\\\n        Not (IsSquare u) := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem sign_ofBijective_pow (p k : Nat) [NeZero p] (hp : p.Prime)\n    (hk : Function.Bijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k)) :\n    (Equiv.Perm.sign (Equiv.ofBijective (fun x : ZMod p => x ^ k) hk) : Int) =\n      if p % 4 = 1 /\\ k % 4 = 3 then -1 else 1 := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem sign_transpose (m n : Nat) :\n    (Equiv.Perm.sign ((finProdFinEquiv.symm.trans (Equiv.prodComm (Fin m) (Fin n))).trans\n        (finProdFinEquiv.trans (finCongr (Nat.mul_comm n m)))) : Int) =\n      (-1) ^ (Nat.choose m 2 * Nat.choose n 2) := by\n  sorry\n\nend TuringTask\n'


def humanize_scan_module():
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    for cand in [here] + list(here.parents):
        if (cand / "humanize_scan.py").is_file():
            sys.path.insert(0, str(cand))
            import humanize_scan
            return humanize_scan
    raise SystemExit("humanize_scan.py not found in the repository root")


def check():
    for name, text in FILES.items():
        assert hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest() == SHA256[name], name
    for name, text in TEXTS.items():
        bad = sorted({ch for ch in text if ord(ch) > 127 or (ord(ch) < 32 and ch != "\n")})
        assert not bad, (name, bad)
    for name in ("README.md", "lakefile.toml", "StatementAndAxiomsCheck.lean",
                 "TuringTask/Basic.lean", "lean-toolchain", "TuringTask.lean",
                 "lake-manifest.json"):
        assert all(ord(ch) < 128 for ch in FILES[name]), name
    assert 'path = "/opt/mathlib4"' in FILES["lakefile.toml"]
    assert "git =" not in FILES["lakefile.toml"]
    assert '"dir": "/opt/mathlib4"' in FILES["lake-manifest.json"]
    assert FILES["lean-toolchain"] == "leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0-rc1\n"
    basic = FILES["TuringTask/Basic.lean"]
    assert basic.startswith("import Mathlib\nimport TuringTask.Main\n")
    assert basic.replace("import TuringTask.Main\n", "", 1).count("exact ") == 5
    stripped = re.sub(r"  exact [^\n]*\n", "  sorry\n",
                      basic.replace("import TuringTask.Main\n", "", 1))
    assert stripped == PROMPT_BASIC, "Basic.lean differs from the prompt's file"
    joined = "\n".join(v for k, v in FILES.items() if k.endswith(".lean") and "Check" not in k)
    for word in ("sorry", "admit", "native_decide", "axiom", "set_option", "instance", "unsafe",
                 "implemented_by", "extern", "opaque"):
        assert not re.search(r"(?<![A-Za-z_.])" + word + r"\b", joined), word
    for name, text in FILES.items():
        if name.endswith(".lean"):
            for i, line in enumerate(text.split("\n"), 1):
                assert len(line) <= 100, (name, i)
    rows = TEXTS["task29_rubric.csv"].split("\n")
    assert rows[0] == '"ID","Criterion","Weight"' and len(rows) == 7
    assert not TEXTS["task29_rubric.csv"].endswith("\n")
    for i, row in enumerate(rows[1:], 1):
        assert row.startswith(f'"{i}","') and row.endswith('","1"') and row.count('"') == 6
    banned = ("proves", "derives", "works out", "figures out", "computes", "understood",
              "considered", "recognized", "accounted", "clean", "idiomatic", "elegant", "clear",
              "appropriate", "thorough", "correctly", "robust")
    crit = TEXTS["task29_rubric.txt"].lower()
    for word in banned:
        assert not re.search(r"\b" + word + r"\b", crit), word
    assert len(re.findall(r"\bsound\b", crit)) == 5      # only inside the axiom name Quot.sound
    hs = humanize_scan_module()
    pieces = [("explanation", TEXTS["task29_golden_explanation.txt"])]
    pieces += [("criterion %d" % i, c)
               for i, c in enumerate(TEXTS["task29_rubric.txt"].rstrip("\n").split("\n"), 1)]
    for label, text in pieces:
        errors, warnings = hs.scan(text)
        assert not errors and not warnings, (label, errors, warnings)


def main():
    check()
    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    buf = io.BytesIO()
    with zipfile.ZipFile(buf, "w", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
        for name in FILES:
            info = zipfile.ZipInfo(f"{PROJECT}/{name}", date_time=(2026, 10, 14, 0, 0, 0))
            info.compress_type = zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED
            info.external_attr = 0o644 << 16
            z.writestr(info, FILES[name].encode("utf-8"))
    (here / "golden_solution.zip").write_bytes(buf.getvalue())
    print("wrote golden_solution.zip", len(buf.getvalue()), "bytes, sha256",
          hashlib.sha256(buf.getvalue()).hexdigest()[:16])
    for name, text in TEXTS.items():
        with open(here / name, "w", encoding="ascii", newline="\n") as fh:
            fh.write(text)
        print("wrote", name, len(text), "chars, ASCII ok")
    lean = [n for n in FILES if n.startswith("TuringTask/")]
    print("Lean lines:", {n: FILES[n].count("\n") for n in lean},
          "total", sum(FILES[n].count("\n") for n in lean))
    print("check passed: sha256, ASCII, statements, forbidden words, CSV, humanize scan 0/0")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
